rn" /><summary type="html">Crochet hook in hand, the animator slightly raises the eyelid of a clay model sheep in a filmmaking technique as old as cinema, perfected over five decades by Aardman Animations.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN approves resolution in support of map that shows Africa's true size</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ec9bc306a685d49fc3835c48924c278dace0bf66d61a58c4fdd36dfaa18a758</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T16:23:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-un-approves-resolution-in-support-of-map-that-shows-africa-s-true-size--b9a2037ede4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-un-approves-resolution-in-support-of-map-that-shows-africa-s-true-size" /><summary type="html">The United Nations on ‌Friday voted for a shift away from the 16th-century Mercator global map towards one more accurately reflecting countries' true size, a resolution sponsored by African states to counter perceptions that the continent is peripheral.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Rain man’ to the rescue? France’s ex-president Hollande plots unlikely comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fb86ec142cb951529ec5ccfbad04798bc1ec610e98332c61c707b980c345140</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T16:22:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260905-rain-man-france-ex-president-francois-hollande-unlikely-comeback-presidential-election--032340a111f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260905-rain-man-france-ex-president-francois-hollande-unlikely-comeback-presidential-election" /><summary type="html">Once so deeply unpopular he had to give up running for a second term in office, former French president François Hollande has slipped back into the conversation ahead of next year’s Élysée Palace race, hoping voters put off by squabbling candidates will come to see him as a safe – if unexciting – pair of hands after a decade of Emmanuel Macron’s ‘disruptive’ presidency.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese national rescued from Nepal tunnel 10 days after flash flood</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3fb0cd065c95024441dd53f2c8f5dc9722ee151a3d3ee4dc86ba256df587e32</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T16:17:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-chinese-national-rescued-from-nepal-tunnel-10-days-after-flash-flood--33dcb0fd9f22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-chinese-national-rescued-from-nepal-tunnel-10-days-after-flash-flood" /><summary type="html">A Chinese national was pulled alive from a tunnel in Nepal on Saturday, authorities said, 10 ‌days after a wall of ice, rock and mud tore through a Himalayan valley, killing more than 1,300 people.</summary></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Putin, Zelensky order pause in strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b0d0994476bfc8ff8b59c2ec6186e170db4a3a2a77c244568003b454937de12</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T16:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-war-in-ukraine-putin-zelensky-order-pause-in-strikes--5ca619025dae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-war-in-ukraine-putin-zelensky-order-pause-in-strikes" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Saturday ordered a 72-hour pause in strikes on Kyiv as US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Moscow.</summary></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff, Kushner arrive in Moscow for talks on peace in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:640a4effba9db661dfd3bc7d650dba5283de34523591ed7bdce5b486d0229106</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-us-envoys-witkoff-kushner-arrive-in-moscow-for-talks-on-peace-in-ukraine--2c5aee12c5ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-us-envoys-witkoff-kushner-arrive-in-moscow-for-talks-on-peace-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">US special representatives Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner landed in Moscow on Saturday for talks on how to end the ‌war in Ukraine, where they were met by Russian presidential envoy Kirill Dmitriev. Our guest Jamie Smith-Maillet tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Culture of fear within US Defence Department: Slow leakage of dissent against the administration'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8f284222b0104eb41f599df784d3f8d7b98d7526719777526e20321126e40a8</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T15:55:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/culture-of-fear-within-us-defence-department-slow-leakage-of-dissent-against-the-administration--5f477c99c6eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture-of-fear-within-us-defence-department-slow-leakage-of-dissent-against-the-administration" /><summary type="html">Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth. He argues that the turmoil surrounding Pete Hegseth points to a problem much deeper than personnel disputes at the Pentagon: The removal and marginalization of experienced officials, the weakening of professional military education, and the prioritization of political loyalty risk changing the institutional culture through which the US military evaluates strategy and challenges political authority.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris hosts African Diaspora International Film Festival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19bd12ae34045e860571ceb165b7cd024731e69b03112b1094995abfad008d77</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T15:22:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-paris-hosts-african-diaspora-international-film-festival--e0e5ca3d59ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-paris-hosts-african-diaspora-international-film-festival" /><summary type="html">This weekend, Paris is hosting the 16th edition of FIFDA, the African Diaspora International Film Festival.
 
From September 4 to 6, 15 films from 13 countries will be screened, spanning fiction and non-fiction, as well as feature-length and short films. The festival provides a space to explore how contemporary societies face and overcome wounds from the past, while giving a voice to members of African diasporas.
 
Guest Lawrence Cole, co-executive producer of "Shadow of Greed", and Diarah N'Daw-Spech, FIFDA co-founder and co-director.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uber announces immediate withdrawal from Nigeria and Uganda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df2d88eda5d9ffcc00d003ff50f760e594bc0b1b9f9a4af32a3c77e25da12387</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T15:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-uber-announces-immediate-withdrawal-from-nigeria-and-uganda--7f61f7a11aa0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-uber-announces-immediate-withdrawal-from-nigeria-and-uganda" /><summary type="html">Uber has announced its immediate withdrawal from Nigeria and Uganda. The decision comes amid a global restructuring, but mainly as Uber has lost significant ground to its competitors in both countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN experts urge Sudan-wide arms embargo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a1d697e50a17653100e73999c3a2da993b77f1a50bd2f58e596d980723cac4c</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T15:16:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-un-experts-urge-sudan-wide-arms-embargo--aef053eaf4c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-un-experts-urge-sudan-wide-arms-embargo" /><summary type="html">A weapons embargo must be extended to the whole of Sudan, and it must be enforced. That is, in essence, the conclusion of a UN experts' report presented to the Human Rights Council. The report also points to the responsibility of foreign entities in a conflict that has now been raging for more than three years. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more.</summary></entry></feed>
